  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 110 PM MDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nHigh pressure in place through the next week for generally dry\nconditions. Sunday appears to be the warmest day of the period,\nand temperatures could approach or exceed record highs in a few\nlocations. With Monday in reach of the shorter-term models, we\nare seeing increased signal for moisture rotating north around\nthe center of the high parked over Utah by that afternoon.\nEnsembles still look fairly dry, with NBM following along with\nno QPF generated anywhere within the CWA. We have to bump up to\nthe Max percentiles in the NBM to see any QPF generated for\nMonday and Monday night, but that lends some credence to the\nsignal. Given that some of these models have been persistent\nwith the precipitation chances, we would not be surprised at\nthis point to see the forecast moisten up through the weekend\nfor the Monday time frame, but the chances will likely be\nisolated and light. The ridge does rebound, so dry conditions \nwill round out the remainder of the forecast period.",
